## 1.  Goal Model – Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition / Enquired Info** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|--------------------------------------|--------------|-------------------|
| **G1: Provide Food Service** | Deliver requested meals from the kitchen to an inpatient room, then retrieve any dirty dishes. | `;` | Achieve | “All requested meals are delivered to the inpatient room and all dirty dishes have been removed.” | – | The service consists of a sequence of stages: request reception, door opening, food delivery, and dish retrieval. |
| **G2: Receive Delivery Request** | Receive an order‑by‑order request from the kitchen. | `;` | Perform | – | – | The request must be received before any other activity can start. |
| **G2.1: Query Kitchen Request** | Check whether a new kitchen delivery request is pending. | `-` | Query | `request_available` | AND (with G2.2) | The robot must first know whether there is a request; this is a pure information query. |
| **G2.2: Process Request** | Store the request details and prepare for delivery. | `-` | Perform | – | – | Once the request is known, the robot must store it and set up the delivery plan. |
| **G3: Deliver Food to Room** | Deliver the requested meal to the inpatient room. | `(FALLBACK(G3.1,G3.2); G3.3)` | Perform | “Food has been placed in the room (either on the table or retrieved by a helper).” | – | First try to place the food on the table; if that is impossible the robot falls back to the fetch‑from‑tray method, then it must track the retrieval. |
| **G3.1: Deliver to Table** | Place the meal directly onto the patient’s table. | `-` | Perform | – | – | Requires the robot’s special manipulation skill. |
| **G3.2: Fetch from Tray** | Have the meal removed from the robot’s tray by a human or another robot. | `;` | Perform | “Meal has been removed from the robot’s tray.” | – | The robot must first determine who can fetch the meal and then coordinate with that actor. |
| **G3.2.1: Query Fetcher Availability** | Determine whether the patient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot can fetch the meal. | `-` | Query | `patient_fetchable, companion_present, nurse_present, robot_available` | AND (with G3.2.2) | The robot needs this knowledge before it can ask someone to fetch. |
| **G3.2.2: Coordinate Fetcher** | Ask the chosen actor to retrieve the meal from the tray. | `-` | Perform | – | – | This is the action that actually triggers the fetch. |
| **G3.3: Track Meal Retrieval** | Record which meal was retrieved, when, and from where; alert if a wrong meal is taken. | `-` | Perform | – | – | The robot must keep a log and detect mismatches. |
| **G4: Ensure Door Open** | Open the inpatient room door (robot‑only or with human/robot help). | `-` | Perform | – | – | The robot cannot enter the room otherwise. |
| **G5: Retrieve Dirty Dishes** | Remove any dirty dishes from the inpatient room. | `-` | Perform | – | – | Dish retrieval is part of the overall service. |

